 ('Reading · An infographic in text',info('How a Power Grid Balances Supply and Demand',[('Generation','Plants **feed** electricity into the grid; output must **match demand second by second**.'),('Transmission','**High-voltage lines** carry power over long distances with **low losses**; **substations** step the voltage down.'),('Peak load','Demand **peaks in the early evening**; operators call on **fast-ramping** plants to **meet the peak**.'),('Frequency','Grid frequency is held at **50 or 60 Hz**; a **sustained deviation** signals imbalance and can **trigger protective shutdowns**.'),('Storage','Batteries **absorb** surplus and **release** it when demand **spikes**, **smoothing** the curve.'),('Reliability','Operators plan for the **loss of the largest unit** (the “N-1 rule”), so a single failure does not **cascade**.')],note='Figures vary by country; the principle of continuous balancing is universal.',gloss=[('load','carga'),('ramp','variar a potência'),('cascade','propagar-se em cascata'),('surplus','excedente')])),
 [('Output must match demand continuously.','T','second by second.'),('Substations raise the voltage for local use.','F','step the voltage down.'),('The N-1 rule prepares for the loss of the largest unit.','T','loss of the largest unit.')],
 [('“peak load” = ?',['pico de carga','carga pesada','carga leve'],0,'peak load = demanda máxima.'),('“cascade” (rede) = ?',['propagar-se em cadeia','cair devagar','cascata de água só'],0,'cascade failure = falha em cascata.')],
 G('Descrever sistemas e processos técnicos',['Recurso','Exemplo','Função'],[['presente simples','Plants **feed** electricity into the grid','processo geral'],['voz passiva','Frequency **is held** at 50 Hz','agente irrelevante'],['verbos de causa','a deviation **can trigger** shutdowns','relação causal'],['contraste de variação','demand **peaks**, batteries **smooth** the curve','dinâmica'],['finalidade','operators plan for N-1 **so that** one failure does not cascade','razão']],'Infográficos técnicos usam **presente simples**, **passiva** e **verbos de causa e efeito** (*trigger, lead to, result in*). Cada item cabe numa linha.',warn='*Tension* (tensão elétrica) também se diz *voltage*; evite *tension* em engenharia elétrica em inglês.'),
 [('Output must ___ demand second by second. (match)','match','verbo técnico.',None),('Frequency ___ held at 50 or 60 Hz. (be)','is','passiva.',None),('A deviation can ___ protective shutdowns. (trigger)','trigger','causa.',None),('Batteries ___ the curve. (smooth)','smooth','verbo de efeito.',None)],
 V('electricity network=rede de eletricidade|baseload plant=usina de carga de base|peaking plant=usina de ponta|high-voltage line=linha de alta tensão|step-down transformer=transformador abaixador|grid frequency=frequência da rede|load curve=curva de carga|demand response=resposta da demanda|spinning reserve=reserva girante|power ramping limit=limite de variação de potência|black start=partida a frio da rede|N-1 criterion=critério N-1|cascading failure=falha em cascata|load shedding=corte de carga|grid inertia=inércia da rede|reactive power=potência reativa|power factor=fator de potência|interconnector=interligação|distribution feeder=alimentador de distribuição|interval meter=medidor de intervalo|battery storage=armazenamento em baterias|pumped hydro=hidrelétrica reversível|curtailment=limitação de geração|capacity margin=margem de capacidade|system operator=operador do sistema|grid congestion=congestionamento da rede|renewable penetration=penetração de renováveis|dispatch order=ordem de despacho|outage window=janela de interrupção|total grid collapse=colapso total da rede'),
 ('Control room',[('Operator','Demand peaks at six o’clock.','A demanda atinge o pico às seis.'),('Engineer','We call the fast-ramping plants to meet it.','Acionamos as usinas de resposta rápida para atendê-la.'),('Operator','And if the largest unit fails?','E se a maior unidade falhar?'),('Engineer','The N-1 rule keeps the grid stable.','A regra N-1 mantém a rede estável.')]),
 [('Explain what a substation does.','Explique.','A substation steps the voltage down for local use.'),('Explain why frequency matters.','Explique.','A sustained deviation can trigger shutdowns.'),('Describe the peak.','Descreva.','Demand peaks in the early evening.')],
 ('Write a 6-sentence description of a technical system you know (water supply, internet, metro), using present simple, passive and causal verbs.','A city’s water is drawn from reservoirs and treated at central plants. Pressure is maintained by pumps and elevated tanks. In heavy rain, the sewer network can overflow and trigger flooding. Engineers monitor flows so that a single burst pipe does not leave districts dry. Demand peaks in the morning. Reserves smooth the curve.',['Usei **passiva**','Usei **trigger/lead to**','Descrevi **um pico**'],'6 frases'),
